WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.370 --> 01:34.920
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.340 --> 01:37.770
[Episode 60]

4
01:38.490 --> 01:41.610
Since October 20, 1936,

5
01:41.920 --> 01:43.350
the Kuomintang forces concentrated

6
01:43.350 --> 01:44.920
nearly 20 divisions

7
01:44.940 --> 01:47.170
under the Tongwei Campaign Plan and launched a full-scale offensive

8
01:47.170 --> 01:50.700
against the Shaanxi-Gansu-Ningxia Revolutionary Base Area.

9
01:50.920 --> 01:51.710
At the time,

10
01:52.000 --> 01:54.789
the campaign to seize Ningxia had yet to begin.

11
01:55.200 --> 01:57.640
To turn the tide, the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

12
01:57.640 --> 01:58.710
hastily drew up

13
01:58.710 --> 02:00.770
the Haiyuan-Dalachi Campaign Plan.

14
02:01.000 --> 02:02.640
However, because Zhang Guotao insisted

15
02:02.640 --> 02:05.020
on the retreat of the Fourth Red Army and the 31st Red Army,

16
02:05.020 --> 02:06.970
it could not be realized.

17
02:07.590 --> 02:08.910
On October 31,

18
02:09.060 --> 02:11.110
the Kuomintang army advanced to Jingyuan,

19
02:11.110 --> 02:13.240
Dalachi, Zhongwei, and other places,

20
02:13.290 --> 02:15.000
cutting off the headquarters of the 4th Front Army

21
02:15.000 --> 02:16.620
that had crossed the Yellow River earlier,

22
02:16.620 --> 02:19.620
as well as the 5th, 9th, and 30th Red Armies,

23
02:19.800 --> 02:21.590
from the 1st and 2nd Front Armies

24
02:21.590 --> 02:23.310
and the 4th and 31st Red Armies

25
02:23.310 --> 02:26.430
still on the east bank of the Yellow River.

26
02:26.680 --> 02:28.840
According to the changing situation, the CPC Central Committee

27
02:28.840 --> 02:30.280
decided on November 8

28
02:30.280 --> 02:33.010
to abandon the campaign plan to capture Ningxia.

29
02:33.630 --> 02:36.430
The main force of the 4th Front Army that had already crossed the Yellow River westward,

30
02:36.430 --> 02:38.079
numbering over 21,000 people,

31
02:38.079 --> 02:41.280
formed the Western Route Army on November 11.

32
02:41.280 --> 02:44.590
The soldiers of the Red Army's Western Route Army fought a tragic and heroic battle all the way,

33
02:44.590 --> 02:46.430
displaying indomitable courage

34
02:46.430 --> 02:49.360
and an unwavering spirit in the face of immense hardship.

35
02:49.360 --> 02:51.750
It reflects the spirit of heroic dedication

36
02:51.750 --> 02:53.500
to the Party and the people,

37
02:54.079 --> 02:56.560
which is in the same vein as the Long March spirit

38
02:56.560 --> 02:58.450
and will go down in history forever.

39
02:58.450 --> 03:00.980
In mid-November 1936,

40
03:01.090 --> 03:03.400
taking into account the enemy and friendly forces' positions, the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

41
03:02.530 --> 03:06.520
[Gansu, Helianwan]

42
03:03.430 --> 03:05.800
decided to launch the Battle of Shanchengbao,

43
03:05.800 --> 03:08.870
concentrating all Red Army forces in the Shaan-Gan-Ning Base Area

44
03:08.870 --> 03:11.190
following the reunion of the three armies.

45
03:11.190 --> 03:12.520
To better coordinate

46
03:12.520 --> 03:15.030
the troops of the 1st, 2nd, and 4th Front Armies

47
03:15.030 --> 03:16.560
in executing the campaign plan,

48
03:16.560 --> 03:18.680
the Central Committee specially dispatched Zhou Enlai to

49
03:18.680 --> 03:21.050
the location of the campaign's frontline general headquarters,

50
03:21.050 --> 03:21.900
Helianwan,

51
03:21.920 --> 03:23.310
to meet with Zhu De, Liu Bocheng,

52
03:23.310 --> 03:26.280
and the leaders of the 2nd and 4th Front Armies.

53
03:27.280 --> 03:29.340
Vice Chairman Zhou, Commander Peng.

54
03:31.560 --> 03:32.370
Enlai.

55
03:33.770 --> 03:34.700
Commander Peng.

56
03:34.720 --> 03:37.320
Thank you for your hard work, Comrade Bocheng.

57
03:40.710 --> 03:41.750
You're back.

58
03:43.180 --> 03:44.900
[Zuo Quan, Acting Commander of the 1st Army Corps, 1st Front Red Army] [Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Army Corps, 1st Front Red Army]

59
03:44.560 --> 03:45.320
Peng.

60
03:46.120 --> 03:46.980
Commander-in-Chief.

61
03:46.980 --> 03:47.770
We meet again.

62
03:47.770 --> 03:48.540
You've had a hard journey.

63
03:48.540 --> 03:49.940
Knowing we'd meet today,

64
03:50.260 --> 03:51.840
the Commander-in-Chief was so excited last night

65
03:51.840 --> 03:53.370
that he didn't sleep a wink.

66
03:54.020 --> 03:56.210
Commander-in-Chief, this battle of ours

67
03:56.210 --> 03:58.650
is truly a joint action of the three armies.

68
03:59.170 --> 04:00.970
It's all under your command.

69
04:00.990 --> 04:02.720
We must fight this battle well.

70
04:03.400 --> 04:04.400
Rest assured.

71
04:05.760 --> 04:07.020
Good, Commander Peng.

72
04:07.520 --> 04:08.580
Comrade Rongzhen.

73
04:08.740 --> 04:09.360
Chief of Staff.

74
04:09.360 --> 04:10.360
Comrade Bocheng.

75
04:10.380 --> 04:11.050
Zuo Quan.

76
04:11.080 --> 04:12.680
Thank you for your hard work.

77
04:17.050 --> 04:17.860
Enlai.

78
04:18.310 --> 04:19.250
You've had a hard journey.

79
04:19.250 --> 04:20.980
General Political Commissar.

80
04:22.040 --> 04:24.720
What did you call me?

81
04:25.040 --> 04:26.380
General Political Commissar.

82
04:26.380 --> 04:29.110
This is the Central Committee's respect for you.

83
04:42.440 --> 04:43.700
Commander-in-Chief.

84
04:45.390 --> 04:48.520
The Commander-in-Chief has been thinking of everyone.

85
04:50.570 --> 04:52.230
The Second Front Army is here.

86
05:10.050 --> 05:10.910
Comrade Enlai.

87
05:12.990 --> 05:14.350
Comrade Enlai.

88
05:14.680 --> 05:15.610
Comrade He Long.

89
05:15.720 --> 05:16.600
I didn't expect

90
05:16.680 --> 05:18.900
to see my old friends from the Nanchang Uprising again.

91
05:18.900 --> 05:20.100
It's been a long time.

92
05:20.310 --> 05:21.200
Do you still remember?

93
05:21.200 --> 05:22.630
My party admission ceremony back then

94
05:22.630 --> 05:25.160
was held on the way south during the Nanchang Uprising.

95
05:25.160 --> 05:26.560
You were the host.

96
05:26.710 --> 05:27.610
Of course I remember.

97
05:27.610 --> 05:29.240
I also remember that to join the party,

98
05:29.240 --> 05:30.970
you applied more than 70 times.

99
05:31.310 --> 05:32.880
I've lost count,

100
05:32.900 --> 05:35.030
but it was definitely dozens of times.

101
05:36.280 --> 05:36.960
Commander-in-Chief Zhu.

102
05:36.960 --> 05:38.500
You've worked hard all the way.

103
05:38.500 --> 05:39.540
It's been hard.

104
05:40.700 --> 05:42.930
Commander-in-Chief Peng, you're finally here.

105
05:42.930 --> 05:44.390
You've had a hard journey.

106
05:44.480 --> 05:45.480
It wasn't easy.

107
05:48.510 --> 05:49.730
Comrade Bishi, Comrade Rongzhen.

108
05:49.730 --> 05:50.860
You've worked hard.

109
05:50.880 --> 05:51.680
Comrade He Long,

110
05:51.680 --> 05:52.580
we haven't met since the Liusha Meeting.

111
05:52.580 --> 05:53.320
Finally, we're together again.

112
05:53.320 --> 05:54.120
Indeed.

113
05:55.659 --> 05:56.409
Comrade Guotao.

114
05:56.409 --> 05:57.340
Comrade He Long.

115
05:57.720 --> 05:58.700
You've worked hard.

116
05:58.700 --> 06:00.500
Not at all. Welcome back.

117
06:08.610 --> 06:09.390
Comrade Enlai.

118
06:09.390 --> 06:09.860
Bishi.

119
06:09.880 --> 06:11.340
You've had a hard journey.

120
06:15.040 --> 06:16.240
Second Young Master?

121
06:16.560 --> 06:17.310
Second Young Master.

122
06:17.310 --> 06:17.920
You've worked hard.

123
06:17.920 --> 06:18.720
Not at all.

124
06:19.560 --> 06:20.760
Second Young Master.

125
06:23.040 --> 06:23.700
Dongsheng.

126
06:23.890 --> 06:24.550
Dongsheng.

127
06:25.240 --> 06:27.370
Long time no see, Second Young Master.

128
06:27.380 --> 06:28.040
Dongsheng.

129
06:28.430 --> 06:28.950
Second Young Master.

130
06:28.950 --> 06:29.510
No, no.

131
06:29.730 --> 06:31.270
Don't call me Second Young Master now.

132
06:31.270 --> 06:32.330
At a time like this,

133
06:32.620 --> 06:34.350
you should call me Comrade now.

134
06:35.659 --> 06:36.720
Comrade Chen Geng.

135
06:37.050 --> 06:38.260
We finally meet.

136
06:39.030 --> 06:40.490
Let me introduce him to the leaders.

137
06:40.490 --> 06:43.370
This is Comrade Lu Dongsheng, who grew up with me.

138
06:43.210 --> 06:45.220
[Lu Dongsheng, Commander of the 4th Division, 2nd Red Army]

139
06:43.400 --> 06:44.860
He is a Division Commander now.

140
06:44.860 --> 06:45.680
Greetings, leaders.

141
06:45.680 --> 06:46.360
Report.

142
06:46.600 --> 06:47.510
My fighting skills

143
06:47.510 --> 06:49.480
were learned from Comrade Chen Geng.

144
06:49.480 --> 06:50.610
He is flattering me.

145
06:50.720 --> 06:51.800
You worked hard yourself.

146
06:51.800 --> 06:52.870
Not at all.

147
06:54.030 --> 06:55.310
What happened to your leg?

148
06:55.310 --> 06:56.110
It's nothing.

149
06:56.240 --> 06:57.640
We fought a battle in Hunan last year,

150
06:57.640 --> 06:58.460
and it hasn't fully healed.

151
06:58.460 --> 06:59.050
So,

152
06:59.250 --> 07:01.710
He Bingyan calls me Lu the Cripple every day.

153
07:02.350 --> 07:04.950
He was the one who called me 'One-armed' first.

154
07:06.230 --> 07:06.920
On the battlefield,

155
07:06.920 --> 07:08.160
we are afraid of nothing.

156
07:08.160 --> 07:10.750
Bullets can only destroy our bodies,

157
07:10.810 --> 07:12.670
but they cannot destroy our will.

158
07:12.980 --> 07:14.660
I promise you, leaders,

159
07:14.920 --> 07:16.360
as long as we are alive,

160
07:16.750 --> 07:18.160
we will fight them to the end.

161
07:18.160 --> 07:18.870
Fight to the end!

162
07:18.870 --> 07:19.360
Good.

163
07:19.380 --> 07:20.580
Chen Geng is right.

164
07:20.720 --> 07:21.630
Comrade Enlai.

165
07:21.630 --> 07:22.720
I have already discussed it with Comrade Bishi

166
07:22.720 --> 07:25.040
and Comrade Xiangying.

167
07:25.070 --> 07:27.830
The 2nd Front Army will be under the command of Commander-in-Chief Peng.

168
07:27.830 --> 07:30.270
We firmly obey the Central Committee's decision.

169
07:30.270 --> 07:31.070
Good.

170
07:31.570 --> 07:33.120
General Political Commissar.

171
07:33.120 --> 07:34.320
What is your opinion?

172
07:37.290 --> 07:38.490
I have no objections.

173
07:39.200 --> 07:41.810
I will follow the Central Committee's arrangements.

174
07:41.810 --> 07:42.610
Good.

175
07:43.240 --> 07:44.070
Comrades.

176
07:44.970 --> 07:47.920
This reunion of our Front Armies

177
07:48.190 --> 07:50.830
is all about standing united

178
07:51.159 --> 07:53.250
and winning this crucial battle.

179
07:53.500 --> 07:54.260
Good.

180
08:07.810 --> 08:11.570
From November 17 to 22, 1936,

181
08:12.160 --> 08:14.870
the 1st, 2nd, and 4th Front Armies of the Red Army,

182
08:14.870 --> 08:17.200
under the unified command of Peng Dehuai,

183
08:17.430 --> 08:21.560
fought continuously in the Shanchengbao area of Huanxian County, Gansu.

184
08:21.630 --> 08:24.090
In total, more than one regiment of the Kuomintang's 78th Division

185
08:24.090 --> 08:25.820
under Hu Zongnan was wiped out.

186
08:26.480 --> 08:29.120
The Kuomintang army was forced to retreat across the board to

187
08:29.120 --> 08:30.950
Dashuikeng, Mengcheng,

188
08:30.980 --> 08:33.299
Tianshuibao, and the areas to the west.

189
08:33.880 --> 08:35.240
The Battle of Shanchengbao

190
08:35.240 --> 08:37.720
was the first major victory achieved

191
08:37.740 --> 08:38.690
through coordinated operations

192
08:38.690 --> 08:41.700
after the three main forces of the Red Army joined forces.

193
08:41.700 --> 08:44.250
It laid the foundation for the Chinese revolution in the Northwest

194
08:44.250 --> 08:46.610
and made a significant contribution to its cause.

195
08:46.610 --> 08:47.890
After the battle,

196
08:48.130 --> 08:49.820
Zhu De and Zhang Guotao

197
08:49.850 --> 08:52.780
led the Red Army headquarters to Zhidan County

198
08:52.920 --> 08:54.560
to join the Central Committee.

199
08:54.240 --> 08:58.540
[Shaanxi, Zhidan County (formerly Bao'an County)]

200
09:03.320 --> 09:04.120
They are here!

201
09:18.930 --> 09:20.190
Commander-in-Chief!

202
09:21.380 --> 09:22.170
Mao!

203
09:22.210 --> 09:23.740
Commander-in-Chief. Mao.

204
09:29.190 --> 09:30.000
Mao!

205
09:45.870 --> 09:46.660
Mao.

206
09:47.990 --> 09:49.250
We are together again.

207
09:53.170 --> 09:55.100
You've worked hard.

208
09:55.160 --> 09:58.250
It's worth it. As long as we can be together again,

209
09:59.250 --> 10:00.580
no hardship is too much.

210
10:00.830 --> 10:02.120
Zhu and Mao.

211
10:02.790 --> 10:04.020
We will never be separated again.

212
10:04.020 --> 10:04.970
Never.

213
10:05.000 --> 10:07.430
I have a few words for the Commander-in-Chief.

214
10:07.430 --> 10:09.160
His magnanimity is as vast as the sea,

215
10:09.160 --> 10:10.700
and his will is as strong as steel.

216
10:10.700 --> 10:11.870
Good, good, good.

217
10:17.760 --> 10:19.490
General Political Commissar.

218
10:19.630 --> 10:20.910
The cadres of our Central Committee

219
10:20.910 --> 10:24.020
and the student representatives of the Red Army University

220
10:24.020 --> 10:25.620
have all come to welcome you.

221
10:28.190 --> 10:29.120
Comrade Guotao.

222
10:32.440 --> 10:33.690
It's good that you are back.

223
10:33.690 --> 10:34.890
Welcome to the North.

224
10:38.950 --> 10:40.060
You're finally back.

225
10:40.060 --> 10:41.320
Commander-in-Chief.

226
10:42.080 --> 10:43.440
Commander-in-Chief Zhu, you've worked hard.

227
10:43.440 --> 10:44.320
Hello, hello.

228
10:45.160 --> 10:47.510
I met Xu Haidong in Dalachi.

229
10:48.390 --> 10:50.030
He said the people here

230
10:50.510 --> 10:52.310
all say you are the great savior.

231
10:53.690 --> 10:55.220
The great savior is not me,

232
10:55.250 --> 10:58.720
but our united Party and Red Army.

233
11:00.680 --> 11:01.610
Comrade Guotao.

234
11:03.630 --> 11:04.490
Comrade Luofu.

235
11:06.000 --> 11:06.840
Welcome home.

236
11:07.230 --> 11:08.040
Thank you.

237
11:08.630 --> 11:09.560
Comrade Guotao.

238
11:09.850 --> 11:10.980
You've worked hard.

239
11:12.360 --> 11:13.560
Good to see you again.

240
11:14.130 --> 11:14.860
Have a seat.

241
11:21.600 --> 11:22.860
Where is my cigarette?

242
11:43.670 --> 11:44.720
Let's share

243
11:45.740 --> 11:47.270
this cigarette, half each.

244
12:13.540 --> 12:15.540
In early April 1938,

245
12:15.950 --> 12:17.820
Zhang Guotao, then acting chairman

246
12:17.820 --> 12:19.720
of the Shaanxi-Gansu-Ningxia Border Region Government,

247
12:19.720 --> 12:21.700
took the opportunity of attending the ceremony to worship

248
12:21.700 --> 12:23.160
the Yellow Emperor's Mausoleum to secretly defect.

249
12:23.160 --> 12:26.270
He soon joined the Kuomintang's secret service organization,

250
12:26.270 --> 12:29.210
the Bureau of Investigation and Statistics of the Military Council,

251
12:29.210 --> 12:31.930
and engaged in anti-communist espionage activities.

252
12:31.930 --> 12:34.400
On April 18, 1938,

253
12:34.530 --> 12:38.430
the CPC Central Committee expelled Zhang Guotao from Party membership.

254
12:38.430 --> 12:41.150
On a cold winter night in 1979,

255
12:41.570 --> 12:43.740
Zhang Guotao died of illness

256
12:43.770 --> 12:46.530
in a nursing home in Toronto, Canada.

257
12:47.510 --> 12:49.080
After the Battle of Shanchengbao,

258
12:49.080 --> 12:52.080
pushing for the Anti-Japanese National United Front

259
12:52.250 --> 12:54.180
had become the top priority for the Party and the Red Army

260
12:54.180 --> 12:56.580
in opening up a new chapter.

261
12:57.210 --> 12:59.660
As early as September 1, 1936,

262
12:59.770 --> 13:01.500
before the Long March was over,

263
13:01.570 --> 13:03.500
the CPC Central Committee issued

264
13:03.520 --> 13:06.780
the Directive on Forcing Chiang Kai-shek to Resist Japan,

265
13:06.900 --> 13:10.260
shifting its general policy from opposing Chiang

266
13:10.280 --> 13:12.470
to urging him to resist Japan.

267
13:12.970 --> 13:14.570
On October 26,

268
13:14.590 --> 13:17.630
four days after the three main Red Army forces reunited,

269
13:17.630 --> 13:20.590
Mao Zedong, together with 45 Red Army generals,

270
13:20.720 --> 13:22.840
sent a telegram to Chiang Kai-shek and others,

271
13:22.840 --> 13:26.430
declaring that if the Kuomintang government was determined to resist Japanese aggression,

272
13:26.430 --> 13:28.560
the Red Army was ready to lead the fight

273
13:28.600 --> 13:31.270
and pledged to cooperate with them to the very end.

274
13:31.270 --> 13:33.580
Chiang Kai-shek ignored the appeal.

275
13:34.880 --> 13:37.290
On December 1, 1936,

276
13:37.570 --> 13:40.100
Mao Zedong, together with Zhu De, Zhou Enlai,

277
13:40.100 --> 13:43.610
Peng Dehuai, He Long, Ren Bishi and 13 others,

278
13:43.890 --> 13:46.110
as well as all Red Army officers and soldiers,

279
13:46.110 --> 13:48.340
once again wrote to Chiang Kai-shek, declaring:

280
13:48.340 --> 13:50.430
"Today, there are only two choices:

281
13:50.460 --> 13:53.100
resist Japan or surrender to Japan.

282
13:53.370 --> 13:56.540
We sincerely hope that future generations will never

283
13:56.560 --> 13:58.110
have to gather and say,

284
13:58.400 --> 14:00.520
'It was none other than Chiang Kai-shek

285
14:00.520 --> 14:02.350
who brought about China's downfall.'

286
14:02.350 --> 14:05.260
With public sentiment and the morale of the troops so clearly against you,

287
14:05.260 --> 14:08.780
why not reflect on the reasons in the quiet of the night?"

288
14:09.050 --> 14:11.980
Chiang Kai-shek still gave no response

289
14:12.000 --> 14:14.130
to this heartfelt and sincere letter.

290
14:14.400 --> 14:16.390
Instead, he pressured Zhang Xueliang and Yang Hucheng

291
14:16.390 --> 14:17.450
to speed up troop deployments

292
14:17.450 --> 14:20.200
and continue their campaign against the Communists.

293
14:20.200 --> 14:21.390
Eleven days later,

294
14:21.890 --> 14:25.130
the Xi'an Incident that shocked China and the world broke out.

295
14:25.130 --> 14:28.000
Zhang Xueliang and Yang Hucheng sent a telegram to the whole country

296
14:28.000 --> 14:29.660
and invited the CPC Central Committee

297
14:29.660 --> 14:32.540
to send representatives to Xi'an to discuss a way forward.

298
14:32.540 --> 14:36.200
The CPC Central Committee immediately held a Politburo meeting.

299
14:36.350 --> 14:39.330
At the meeting, Mao Zedong delivered an important speech,

300
14:39.330 --> 14:41.110
offering a calm and comprehensive analysis of the nature

301
14:41.110 --> 14:43.950
and prospects of the Xi'an Incident,

302
14:43.980 --> 14:47.570
as well as how to deal with Chiang Kai-shek.

303
14:47.970 --> 14:49.290
On December 17,

304
14:49.840 --> 14:52.940
Zhou Enlai arrived in Xi'an on behalf of the CPC Central Committee

305
14:52.940 --> 14:54.690
and conveyed the Party's position

306
14:54.690 --> 14:56.690
to Zhang Xueliang and Yang Hucheng.

307
14:56.860 --> 14:59.130
The two sides agreed on six principles

308
14:59.160 --> 15:01.520
for a peaceful resolution of the Xi'an Incident.

309
15:01.290 --> 15:04.390
[Shaanxi, Xi'an, Gao Guizi's Residence]

310
15:14.270 --> 15:16.510
You always have to eat.

311
15:20.690 --> 15:23.400
Hanqing (Zhang Xueliang) sent a set of dentures.

312
15:23.400 --> 15:25.330
Please, just have a bite.

313
15:41.930 --> 15:43.480
Hanqing is here to see you.

314
15:47.270 --> 15:48.200
Come in.

315
15:53.400 --> 15:54.680
Come in.

316
16:04.500 --> 16:05.590
Zhang Xueliang!

317
16:05.900 --> 16:08.100
From now on, there'll be no place for you

318
16:08.290 --> 16:10.050
anywhere in China!

319
16:24.600 --> 16:25.530
Generalissimo.

320
16:28.390 --> 16:29.150
Brother.

321
16:31.930 --> 16:32.680
Brother,

322
16:34.300 --> 16:36.220
I am not kneeling for myself.

323
16:37.500 --> 16:40.160
It's for the 30 million people in the Northeast.

324
16:41.150 --> 16:42.300
For years,

325
16:43.120 --> 16:46.540
the pain of national humiliation and personal loss has weighed heavily on me.

326
16:46.540 --> 16:49.050
The Northeast has been occupied for five years.

327
16:49.050 --> 16:50.050
Five years.

328
16:51.550 --> 16:52.690
The men of the Northeastern Army

329
16:52.690 --> 16:55.490
have longed to march north every single day.

330
16:56.050 --> 16:57.810
The Japanese have already extended their reach

331
16:57.810 --> 17:00.930
from the Northeast into North China.

332
17:01.170 --> 17:04.569
Their guns are trained on Peiping.

333
17:06.180 --> 17:11.310
Hundreds of thousands of national troops are fighting the Communists in northern Shaanxi.

334
17:12.030 --> 17:13.030
Brother.

335
17:13.720 --> 17:15.510
Once we've finished fighting among ourselves,

336
17:15.510 --> 17:17.960
who's left to fight the Japanese?

337
17:20.359 --> 17:21.640
If this continues,

338
17:22.490 --> 17:24.220
will our country even survive?

339
17:25.319 --> 17:26.880
If the country perishes,

340
17:26.900 --> 17:30.130
you, me, and all the soldiers of the Party

341
17:30.160 --> 17:32.790
will go down in history as sinners.

342
17:33.200 --> 17:34.440
When that time comes,

343
17:34.970 --> 17:36.630
can you feel at ease, Brother?

344
17:37.120 --> 17:38.710
When that time comes,

345
17:39.190 --> 17:42.280
how will history judge you?

346
17:43.080 --> 17:44.280
When that time comes,

347
17:44.830 --> 17:49.720
can you bear the blame for the subjugation of our nation?

348
17:49.740 --> 17:51.230
When what time comes!

349
17:51.640 --> 17:52.790
Let me ask you.

350
17:53.090 --> 17:55.200
Right now,

351
17:55.890 --> 17:56.680
have they

352
17:58.470 --> 18:00.510
already arrived?

353
18:02.240 --> 18:05.680
Zhou Enlai arrived in Xi'an a few days ago.

354
18:08.180 --> 18:10.380
In the bounty I issued,

355
18:10.430 --> 18:13.300
Zhou Enlai's head is worth 30,000 silver dollars.

356
18:14.100 --> 18:16.430
How much would my head be worth

357
18:16.780 --> 18:18.310
if you left it here in Xi'an?

358
18:18.640 --> 18:20.850
I went against your will, Brother,

359
18:21.440 --> 18:23.440
because I had no other choice.

360
18:23.970 --> 18:27.060
But I have no selfish motives in doing this,

361
18:27.300 --> 18:28.610
nor any personal gain.

362
18:29.000 --> 18:31.610
Stop putting on an act here.

363
18:41.730 --> 18:44.360
How could political matters come to this?

364
18:44.790 --> 18:47.310
I came to Xi'an for only one purpose,

365
18:47.330 --> 18:51.090
which is to bring your brother back to Nanjing safely.

366
18:51.400 --> 18:54.010
Zhang Hanqing, I'm telling you.

367
18:54.360 --> 18:56.190
I brought a gun

368
18:57.200 --> 18:58.440
and gave it to Donald.

369
18:58.750 --> 19:00.140
If anyone makes a move,

370
19:00.890 --> 19:03.160
blood will be spilled in Xi'an.

371
19:04.000 --> 19:04.930
I, Song Meiling,

372
19:06.720 --> 19:08.400
always keep my word.

373
19:15.490 --> 19:16.820
I'm to blame for

374
19:17.850 --> 19:19.570
putting you through this, Brother.

375
19:19.570 --> 19:20.720
As long as I am here,

376
19:21.010 --> 19:22.960
I will keep you two safe.

377
19:25.750 --> 19:28.710
Zhou Enlai has discussed it with me before.

378
19:28.880 --> 19:30.750
They proposed six propositions

379
19:30.770 --> 19:33.110
for the peaceful resolution of this incident,

380
19:33.110 --> 19:35.270
clearly showing the attitude of the CPC.

381
19:35.270 --> 19:38.350
As long as you agree to and implement these terms,

382
19:38.510 --> 19:41.370
the CPC will stand with the Nationalist Government

383
19:41.510 --> 19:42.830
and you

384
19:43.000 --> 19:44.260
in rejecting civil war,

385
19:44.260 --> 19:45.620
resisting Japanese aggression,

386
19:45.620 --> 19:46.650
and joining forces against Japan.

387
19:46.650 --> 19:48.310
Is this what you call uniting?

388
19:48.910 --> 19:50.720
You raised an army in rebellion

389
19:50.850 --> 19:52.380
and defied your superiors.

390
19:52.480 --> 19:55.750
I think you've joined forces with the Communists to force my hand.

391
19:55.750 --> 19:57.810
As long as you decide to resist Japan,

392
19:58.160 --> 19:59.270
after this is over,

393
19:59.530 --> 20:01.920
I will personally escort you

394
20:02.740 --> 20:04.370
back to Nanjing.

395
20:40.420 --> 20:42.310
Don't go back with me.

396
20:43.880 --> 20:45.530
If you go to Nanjing,

397
20:47.490 --> 20:49.220
it will be hard for me to handle.

398
20:52.130 --> 20:53.370
My mind is made up.

399
20:55.440 --> 20:56.200
I

400
20:57.460 --> 20:59.060
will definitely escort you.

401
21:18.970 --> 21:20.020
Hanqing.

402
21:27.190 --> 21:31.040
Thank you for preparing these dentures for me.

403
22:16.660 --> 22:19.470
Mao Zedong said in his letter

404
22:21.090 --> 22:24.090
that I should reflect on myself in the dead of night.

405
22:25.630 --> 22:27.690
I've thought about it for a long time.

406
22:29.200 --> 22:32.920
The purge in 1927 was over

407
22:35.060 --> 22:39.650
nine years ago,

408
22:39.840 --> 22:42.570
and the campaigns against the Communists in 1930

409
22:44.110 --> 22:47.070
began more than six years ago.

410
22:47.310 --> 22:49.200
How many chances have I had

411
22:49.200 --> 22:53.240
to wipe them out once and for all?

412
22:55.720 --> 23:01.110
But every time I missed the opportunity

413
23:01.140 --> 23:03.550
and let them escape.

414
23:04.070 --> 23:05.030
Tell me,

415
23:07.800 --> 23:09.630
is this some hidden design

416
23:11.200 --> 23:12.480
or

417
23:13.490 --> 23:14.570
the will of heaven?

418
23:20.090 --> 23:21.440
Up to now,

419
23:21.620 --> 23:23.820
the bandit problem is still not solved.

420
23:24.400 --> 23:27.250
If even men like these can outmaneuver me

421
23:28.370 --> 23:30.410
and put me in such a predicament,

422
23:30.740 --> 23:33.270
what chance would I stand against Mao Zedong?

423
23:33.550 --> 23:34.920
My dear,

424
23:35.090 --> 23:37.010
is this Mao Zedong

425
23:37.880 --> 23:40.090
my natural enemy?

426
23:41.040 --> 23:43.600
Don't think so much, okay?

427
23:47.610 --> 23:49.440
From the perspective of timing,

428
23:49.660 --> 23:51.420
stopping the civil war

429
23:52.030 --> 23:53.260
and uniting to resist Japan

430
23:53.260 --> 23:55.220
is irresistible.

431
23:56.990 --> 24:00.800
But Mao Zedong saw the will of Heaven

432
24:01.070 --> 24:02.550
and adapted to the changing circumstances.

433
24:02.550 --> 24:05.350
That's how he turned the tide when all seemed lost.

434
24:05.920 --> 24:08.050
Now he goes north to Shaanxi and Gansu,

435
24:08.550 --> 24:10.010
maneuvers in North China,

436
24:10.700 --> 24:12.700
and gains geographical advantages.

437
24:12.700 --> 24:13.830
Zhang and Yang

438
24:14.600 --> 24:15.800
have rebelled

439
24:17.470 --> 24:19.470
and laid everything bare for the whole nation to see.

440
24:19.470 --> 24:22.060
Everyone now knows the truth.

441
24:22.200 --> 24:24.960
Now I have lost the support of the people.

442
24:25.160 --> 24:29.140
What do you mean, the right time, place, and people?

443
24:29.680 --> 24:32.160
So what if you are a prisoner once?

444
24:32.330 --> 24:35.140
Haven't we all heard of enduring humiliation

445
24:35.170 --> 24:36.960
and biding one's time?

446
24:37.110 --> 24:39.720
As long as you can return to Nanjing safely,

447
24:39.740 --> 24:41.170
what we lost today,

448
24:41.200 --> 24:44.050
we can get back one by one.

449
24:51.710 --> 24:53.310
The inchworm bends

450
24:54.160 --> 24:55.510
to stretch forward;

451
24:56.070 --> 24:57.550
the serpent coils

452
24:57.830 --> 24:59.590
to preserve its life.

453
25:00.030 --> 25:01.640
I understand this truth.

454
25:01.960 --> 25:05.440
I, Chiang Kai-shek, will never be defeated.

455
25:06.790 --> 25:09.120
If the Communist Party is not eliminated,

456
25:10.240 --> 25:11.920
I swear I am not a man.

457
25:25.750 --> 25:27.940
You haven't slept for days.

458
25:29.030 --> 25:31.200
Can you take a rest?

459
28:45.300 --> 28:48.300
On December 24, 1936,

460
28:48.610 --> 28:51.080
Chiang Kai-shek accepted the six proposals, including stopping the civil war

461
28:51.080 --> 28:54.080
and uniting with the Communist Party to resist Japan.

462
28:54.370 --> 28:55.290
On the 25th,

463
28:55.540 --> 28:57.100
Chiang Kai-shek was released.

464
28:57.100 --> 28:59.610
Zhang Xueliang ignored Zhou Enlai's dissuasion

465
28:59.610 --> 29:02.880
and insisted on escorting Chiang Kai-shek back to Nanjing.

466
29:02.880 --> 29:06.430
The Xi'an Incident was finally resolved peacefully.

467
29:08.330 --> 29:20.130
[January 13, 1937: The CPC Central Committee, the Central Government of the Chinese Soviet Republic, and the Central Revolutionary Military Commission relocate to Fushi (Yan'an)]

468
29:23.050 --> 29:25.050
The Red Army's Long March

469
29:25.570 --> 29:29.500
fulfilled the strategic objective of marching north to resist Japan,

470
29:29.530 --> 29:32.460
ushering in a new chapter in the Chinese Revolution.

471
29:32.790 --> 29:33.990
The Central Red Army,

472
29:34.000 --> 29:36.680
the 2nd Front Army, the 4th Front Army,

473
29:36.960 --> 29:38.270
and the 25th Red Army

474
29:38.490 --> 29:40.600
fought in 15 provinces in total,

475
29:41.070 --> 29:43.590
traveling more than 65,000 li.

476
29:44.070 --> 29:47.050
They crossed more than 40 high mountains and dangerous peaks,

477
29:47.050 --> 29:50.330
over 20 of which stood above 4,000 meters.

478
29:50.550 --> 29:52.350
They crossed nearly 100 rivers,

479
29:53.020 --> 29:53.650
passed through

480
29:53.650 --> 29:56.640
the vast grasslands known as the forbidden zone of life,

481
29:56.640 --> 29:59.120
pushing the limits of human endurance.

482
29:59.860 --> 30:00.980
During the Long March,

483
30:00.980 --> 30:03.660
more than 600 important battles were fought.

484
30:03.680 --> 30:07.290
Among them, the Central Red Army fought over 380 times,

485
30:07.410 --> 30:10.210
the 2nd Front Army over 120 times,

486
30:10.310 --> 30:12.620
the 4th Front Army over 80 times,

487
30:12.990 --> 30:15.510
and the 25th Red Army over 20 times.

488
30:16.350 --> 30:18.180
At the beginning of the Long March,

489
30:18.180 --> 30:19.680
the total number of Red Army soldiers from all routes

490
30:19.680 --> 30:21.930
was about 186,000.

491
30:22.010 --> 30:24.180
Including the Red Army soldiers supplemented along the way,

492
30:24.180 --> 30:26.940
the total number was over 220,000.

493
30:28.000 --> 30:30.360
When the three main forces of the Red Army joined forces,

494
30:30.360 --> 30:33.070
the Long March Red Army that reached the Shaanxi and Gansu region

495
30:33.070 --> 30:35.900
numbered just over 56,700.

496
30:36.440 --> 30:37.290
Among them,

497
30:37.530 --> 30:41.020
the Central Red Army had 86,000 people at the start of the Long March.

498
30:41.020 --> 30:43.130
Including the troops supplemented along the way,

499
30:43.130 --> 30:44.940
in October 1935,

500
30:44.960 --> 30:48.960
only a little over 7,000 people reached the Shaanxi and Gansu base area.

501
30:49.140 --> 30:50.310
On average, out of more than a dozen

502
30:50.310 --> 30:52.850
Red Army soldiers who participated in the Long March,

503
30:52.850 --> 30:57.050
only one witnessed the victory of the Long March.

504
31:39.510 --> 31:40.420
Runzhi,

505
31:41.670 --> 31:44.230
when our Xinmin Society was founded,

506
31:44.650 --> 31:46.710
we crossed the Xiang River together.

507
31:47.440 --> 31:48.370
Look at you all,

508
31:48.830 --> 31:50.410
young classmates in your prime,

509
31:50.410 --> 31:51.740
full of youthful vigor.

510
31:52.130 --> 31:52.930
Runzhi,

511
31:53.960 --> 31:55.940
once you've had your chance to shape the course of events,

512
31:55.940 --> 32:00.250
[He Shuheng]

513
31:56.160 --> 31:57.890
crossing the Xiang River again

514
31:58.390 --> 32:00.840
will surely feel different.

515
32:16.790 --> 32:17.920
Runzhi.

516
32:18.720 --> 32:21.070
A bosom friend is enough to me;

517
32:21.390 --> 32:24.560
I'll hold the same attitude to the world!

518
32:25.390 --> 32:26.840
When we parted in Yudu,

519
32:27.540 --> 32:30.170
you said you would use your own feet

520
32:30.200 --> 32:31.570
to forge your own path.

521
32:31.810 --> 32:36.180
[Qu Qiubai]

522
32:31.960 --> 32:33.570
Now you have made it out

523
32:34.020 --> 32:35.260
and arrived here.

524
32:36.250 --> 32:38.940
I hope you won't stop.

525
32:50.330 --> 32:51.130
Runzhi,

526
32:52.050 --> 32:53.720
the peasants are our roots.

527
32:54.110 --> 32:55.930
I have already asked someone to send my manuscript

528
32:55.930 --> 32:57.130
to Shanghai.

529
32:57.750 --> 32:59.010
I don't know if you'll be able to see it

530
32:59.010 --> 33:00.580
in the future.

531
33:00.400 --> 33:04.760
[Fang Zhimin]

532
33:00.780 --> 33:01.820
I believe

533
33:03.210 --> 33:04.250
that China

534
33:05.020 --> 33:09.210
will definitely be a lovely country in the future.

535
33:22.770 --> 33:25.600
Brother, the blanket you gave me,

536
33:25.850 --> 33:28.820
I lost it because we left in a hurry on the day of the breakout.

537
33:28.820 --> 33:29.780
What a pity.

538
33:30.730 --> 33:32.660
You won't scold me again, will you?

539
33:32.890 --> 33:36.330
Brother, you have a quick temper. Try to get angry less.

540
33:35.070 --> 33:37.110
[Mao Zetan]

541
33:47.690 --> 33:48.580
Chairman Mao,

542
33:49.030 --> 33:51.310
has the main force crossed the Xiang River?

543
33:51.310 --> 33:52.510
Please rest assured.

544
33:52.650 --> 33:54.020
If the main force doesn't cross the river,

545
33:54.020 --> 33:57.500
[Chen Shuxiang]

546
33:54.090 --> 33:57.600
our 34th Division of the Red Army will fight to the death!

547
34:06.840 --> 34:10.159
[Yi Dangping] [Hong Chao]

548
34:07.390 --> 34:08.120
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

549
34:08.120 --> 34:09.120
Hello, Chairman.

550
34:14.380 --> 34:15.530
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

551
34:14.960 --> 34:18.340
[Huang Kaixiang][Deng Ping]

552
34:16.199 --> 34:17.659
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

553
34:25.469 --> 34:26.360
Chairman Mao.

554
34:26.219 --> 34:29.030
[Qian Zhuangfei]

555
34:26.610 --> 34:30.010
This is the Red Army Martyrs Memorial Tower I newly designed.

556
34:43.239 --> 34:47.130
[Wu Huanxian] [Xun huaizhou]

557
34:44.340 --> 34:45.280
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

558
34:45.280 --> 34:46.739
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

559
34:54.679 --> 34:55.620
Hello, Chairman.

560
34:55.620 --> 34:56.980
Hello, Chairman.

561
34:57.030 --> 34:59.960
[Xia Xi] [Zhang Hui]

562
35:00.010 --> 35:01.210
[Long Yun]

563
35:04.090 --> 35:04.980
[Wang Youjun]

564
35:07.620 --> 35:08.460
Chairman Mao!

565
35:08.640 --> 35:09.560
Chairman Mao.

566
35:09.610 --> 35:12.260
[Guo Shanlin]

567
35:09.710 --> 35:11.230
Hello, Chairman Mao.

568
35:12.260 --> 35:15.400
[Liu Xicai]

569
35:15.400 --> 35:16.870
[Long Yuqin]

570
35:20.970 --> 35:22.170
Hello, Chairman Mao.

571
35:26.790 --> 35:29.270
[Mao Zhenhua]

572
35:26.890 --> 35:28.290
I brought you some chili.

573
35:28.530 --> 35:30.140
I've been saving it.

574
35:33.060 --> 35:35.710
[Hu Changbao]

575
35:33.900 --> 35:34.830
Chairman Mao.

576
35:35.390 --> 35:36.600
You guessed right.

577
35:37.210 --> 35:41.330
What I wrote is that snow is the clouds in the sky.

578
36:10.040 --> 36:10.850
Chairman Mao.

579
36:10.880 --> 36:11.920
Hello, Chairman.

580
36:11.940 --> 36:13.190
Reporting to Chairman Mao,

581
36:13.190 --> 36:14.650
our Western Route Army is currently

582
36:14.650 --> 36:16.670
engaging the enemy in Gaotai County.

583
36:16.670 --> 36:18.310
We will definitely hold our position.

584
36:16.740 --> 36:18.120
[Dong Zhentang]

585
36:18.120 --> 36:21.660
[Yang Keming] [Li Bingren]

586
36:18.370 --> 36:20.300
Rest assured, Central Committee.

587
36:22.310 --> 36:25.280
[Sun Yuqing] [Chen Haisong]

588
36:26.270 --> 36:30.710
[January 20, 1937: Dong Zhentang, Commander of the Fifth Red Army, and Yang Keming, Director of its Political Department, fell heroically in the Battle of Gaotai]

589
36:30.750 --> 36:35.800
[March 12, 1937: Chen Haisong, Political Commissar of the Ninth Red Army, was struck by multiple bullets and died heroically in the Battle of Liyuankou]

590
36:35.840 --> 36:42.180
[March 1937: Li Pingren, Chief of Staff of the Fifth Red Army, died of his wounds while fighting in the Qilian Mountains]

591
36:42.210 --> 36:52.850
[Late May 1937: Sun Yuqing, Commander of the Ninth Red Army, was captured and taken to Xining. He remained steadfast and was executed.]

592
39:44.910 --> 39:45.940
Chairman Mao.

593
39:46.140 --> 39:46.980
Xie.

594
39:48.440 --> 39:51.240
Chairman Mao, are you here to see the Yellow River?

595
39:51.250 --> 39:52.040
Yes.

596
39:53.310 --> 39:54.190
Xie.

597
39:54.990 --> 39:56.520
You've grown taller again.

598
39:59.910 --> 40:03.470
Who made these new cotton shoes for you?

599
40:03.580 --> 40:06.180
An Auntie in Northern Shaanxi made them for me.

600
40:08.450 --> 40:10.380
Chairman Mao, you know what?

601
40:10.640 --> 40:12.550
When I first put on these shoes,

602
40:12.570 --> 40:13.700
they fit perfectly.

603
40:14.110 --> 40:15.720
It's only been a dozen days,

604
40:15.740 --> 40:17.540
and they're already a bit tight.

605
40:17.630 --> 40:19.430
That means you're growing fast.

606
40:19.560 --> 40:21.690
The shoes can't keep up with your feet.

607
40:23.200 --> 40:24.720
Do you remember

608
40:25.270 --> 40:26.620
back in Yeping?

609
40:26.640 --> 40:30.730
your straw sandals were this much bigger than your feet?

610
40:31.210 --> 40:34.650
I remember. My feet were small then,

611
40:34.800 --> 40:36.040
and the shoes were too big.

612
40:36.040 --> 40:39.460
Then do you remember, during the Long March,

613
40:41.100 --> 40:43.560
how many pairs of straw sandals you changed?

614
40:45.570 --> 40:46.930
I don't remember that.

615
40:47.530 --> 40:49.860
I changed a pair every seven or eight days,

616
40:50.040 --> 40:52.300
so it must have been over a hundred pairs.

617
40:52.740 --> 40:54.220
Then can you calculate

618
40:54.630 --> 40:56.580
how many pairs of straw sandals the Red Army used

619
40:56.580 --> 40:59.540
during the Long March?

620
41:01.970 --> 41:03.530
I can't calculate that.

621
41:06.430 --> 41:09.890
Chairman Mao, will we go on another Long March in the future?

622
41:11.130 --> 41:13.130
As long as people live in this world,

623
41:13.320 --> 41:15.030
they will always walk.

624
